Catalog number : I00044
Uniform title: Bhaktotsava
Manuscript : IFP manuscript bundle RE30806
Description: RE30806. Bhaktotsavam. This manuscript comprises a significant work called Bhaktotsava. There are five different topics which have been explained in this bundle: 1. Devyutsavavidhi, 2. Bhaktotsavavidhi, 3. Varṣotsavavidhi, 4. Utsvava-prāyaścittavidhi, and 5. Agnivibhajanam. The chapters are discussed in detail, and occasionally rituals of Goddess Devī and bhakthas (souls that obtained self-realisation and unity with the Lord) are explained from the Lalitāgama and the ceremonial rituals of a year, including monthly, fortnight and full moon day rituals, are explained from Uttarakāmikāgama. The prāyaścittavidhi (act of amends for ritualistic errors) is explained as per the Kāraṇāgama and the ritual Agnivibhajanam performed with the nine divisions of fire (Lord Agni).The bundle contains 39 folios, and the condition is a bit damaged. The size of the folios is 38.8✕3.7 cm, and there are 5 to 7 lines per folio.
